.TH FKSTRVERSION 3 2026-09-24 "fkstring" "fkstring Library Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
fkstrversion, FKSTRING_VERSION, FKSTRING_VERSION_MAJOR, FKSTRING_VERSION_MINOR, FKSTRING_VERSION_PATCH, FKSTRING_VERSION_NUMBER \- fkstring library version
.SH LIBRARY
fkstring library
.RI ( libfkstring ,\~ \-lfkstring )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fkstring.h>
.PP
.B const char *fkstrversion(void);
.PP
.B #define FKSTRING_VERSION_MAJOR
.B #define FKSTRING_VERSION_MINOR
.B #define FKSTRING_VERSION_PATCH
.B #define FKSTRING_VERSION
.B #define FKSTRING_VERSION_NUMBER
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The fkstring package is versioned as
.IR major . minor . patch ,
following Semantic Versioning.
While
.I major
is 0, the API is not yet stable, and any
.I minor
release may change it incompatibly.
.PP
The macros give the version of the
.I <fkstring.h>
a program is compiled against.
.BR FKSTRING_VERSION_MAJOR ,
.BR FKSTRING_VERSION_MINOR ,
and
.B FKSTRING_VERSION_PATCH
are integer constants.
.B FKSTRING_VERSION
is the same version as a string literal, such as
.BR \(dq0.9.0\(dq .
.B FKSTRING_VERSION_NUMBER
is
.IR major \~*\~10000\~+\~ minor \~*\~100\~+\~ patch ,
an integer constant suitable for
.B #if
comparisons.
.PP
.BR fkstrversion ()
returns the version of the library the program is running with.
With a shared library, this can differ from
.B FKSTRING_VERSION
if the library was upgraded after the program was built.
.PP
The package version is separate from the shared library's
.I soname
version
.RI ( libfkstring.so.0 ),
which changes only when the library's binary interface does.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR fkstrversion ()
returns a pointer to a static string in the same format as
.BR FKSTRING_VERSION .
The caller must not modify or free it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
#if FKSTRING_VERSION_NUMBER < 900
#error "fkstring 0.9.0 or later is required"
#endif
\&
if (strcmp(fkstrversion(), FKSTRING_VERSION) != 0)
    fprintf(stderr, "built with fkstring %s, running with %s\en",
            FKSTRING_VERSION, fkstrversion());
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fkstring (3)
